# 低频词汇 List02
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2026恋练有词
# 描述: 低频词汇List02核心词汇

calibrate /ˈkælɪbreɪt/ v. 校准 The equipment must be calibrated before use. 设备使用前必须校准。
canopy /ˈkænəpi/ n. 树冠 The forest canopy provides shade. 森林树冠提供了阴凉。
cascade /kæˈskeɪd/ n./v. 级联 The reforms had a cascade effect on the economy. 改革对经济产生了连锁反应。
catalyst /ˈkætəlɪst/ n. 催化剂 The event was a catalyst for political change. 该事件是政治变革的催化剂。
census /ˈsensəs/ n. 人口普查 The census data reveals demographic trends. 人口普查数据揭示了人口趋势。
certify /ˈsɜːtɪfaɪ/ v. 认证 The product has been certified as safe. 该产品已被认证为安全。
charter /ˈtʃɑːtə(r)/ n. 章程 The organization operates under a formal charter. 该组织在正式章程下运作。
cite /saɪt/ v. 引用 The professor cited multiple sources in the lecture. 教授在讲座中引用了多个来源。
clamp /klæmp/ v./n. 夹紧 The authorities clamped down on illegal trade. 当局严厉打击了非法贸易。
clan /klæn/ n. 家族 The clan has a long history in the region. 该家族在该地区有悠久的历史。
clergy /ˈklɜːdʒi/ n. 神职人员 The clergy offered comfort to the community. 神职人员为社区提供了安慰。
clone /kləʊn/ n./v. 克隆 Scientists successfully cloned the endangered species. 科学家成功克隆了濒危物种。
cluster /ˈklʌstə(r)/ n./v. 集群 The houses clustered around the village center. 房屋聚集在村庄中心周围。
coalition /ˌkəʊəˈlɪʃn/ n. 联合 Several organizations formed a coalition for change. 几个组织组成了变革联盟。
coexist /ˌkəʊɪɡˈzɪst/ v. 共存 Different species coexist in the ecosystem. 不同物种在生态系统中共存。
compile /kəmˈpaɪl/ v. 编纂 The team compiled a comprehensive database. 团队编纂了一个综合数据库。
complementary /ˌkɒmplɪˈmentəri/ adj. 互补的 The two services are complementary. 这两种服务是互补的。
concede /kənˈsiːd/ v. 承认 The politician conceded defeat in the election. 政治家承认在选举中失败。
condemn /kənˈdem/ v. 谴责 The international community condemned the violence. 国际社会谴责了暴力行为。
confide /kənˈfaɪd/ v. 信任 She confided her deepest fears to her therapist. 她向治疗师倾诉了最深的恐惧。
congregate /ˈkɒŋɡrɪɡeɪt/ v. 集合 Protesters congregated in the town square. 抗议者聚集在镇广场。
conquest /ˈkɒŋkwest/ n. 征服 The conquest of space remains a human ambition. 征服太空仍然是人类的雄心。
consecutive /kənˈsekjətɪv/ adj. 连续的 The team won five consecutive championships. 该团队赢得了连续五次冠军。
conspiracy /kənˈspɪrəsi/ n. 阴谋 The police uncovered a conspiracy to commit fraud. 警方发现了一个实施欺诈的阴谋。
constraint /kənˈstreɪnt/ n. 制约 Financial constraints limit the scope of the project. 财务限制了项目的范围。
contempt /kənˈtempt/ n. 藐视 He was held in contempt of court. 他被判藐视法庭。
contend /kənˈtend/ v. 竞争 Several candidates contend for the position. 几名候选人竞争该职位。
contingent /kənˈtɪndʒənt/ adj. 取决于 The deal is contingent on regulatory approval. 该交易取决于监管批准。
contrive /kənˈtraɪv/ v. 设计 The engineer contrived a clever mechanism. 工程师设计了一个巧妙的机制。
convict /kənˈvɪkt/ v./n. 定罪 He was convicted of tax evasion. 他被判犯有逃税罪。
